Hi Mike,

Thanks for your reply!

When I post this question, I was thinking of a lizard species (Phrynocephalus vlangalii) at Qinghai-Tibet plateau. A population at low elevation (~ 2600 m) can thermoregulate between the shrub (or tree sometimes) and open sandy habitat, while a population at high elevation (~ 3600 m) has no large vegetations to use. Both of them can be in full sun, therefore, the min_shade should be 0. However, I think I should set max_shade differently for them.

I have collected field body temperatures of both populations. Should I try different max_shade when calculating body temperatures with NicheMapR and find out which max_shade results in a perfect match between the empirical data and modeling output?

Best,

Liang

